From 1b9df5c2f0b4e4e6b0aedb319e463d8caf6e1700 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:23:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a relay skips every registered synthetic user
 row, a running /loop tick's row and a storeless Kanban notice [daveey]

Review 5878871802 on #1583: _latest_user_message still accepted untyped synthetic
role='user' rows a notice-woken turn writes itself, so verify() named them as
the person's reply.

- The excluded openings now come from the producers' registries:
  agent.conversation_compression_scaffolding._SYNTHETIC_USER_PREFIXES (task-list
  snapshot, background-process notices, [System: nudges), pre_final_gate.HELD_NOTICE,
  the /loop wakeup frame (hermes_cli.loops templates), plus [System: / [System note:
  (auto-continue and interrupted-turn notes) and the session-mentions courier.
- A slash-command /loop tick submits its prompt untyped: while the session's loop
  is awaiting_response, a non-steer row at/after last_fired_at is the loop's.
- The storeless ("unkeyed") Kanban notice fallback now submits its turn with
  display_kind='kanban_notice' (display_text = the row), like every other notice
  wake, so its user row is typed.

Tests: synthetic-row cases for each opening, a slash /loop tick case, a registry
coverage test (gateway/run.py and tui_gateway/session_history.py auto-continue
prefixes read by ast), and the storeless notice turn's display kind. RED on the
previous sources: 9 failed.
